  "description": "The application is for repairs to Silo D, which is a grade II listed building. The works cover:\nOvercovering three flat roofs in liquid applied roofing products.\nIntroduction of a mansafe system to the intermediate roof for future maintenance.\nThe rotten boards covering the chute openings in the lowest headhouse flat roof (number 3 on the drawing), will be replaced with new marine ply and lead.\nRepairs and unblocking of rainwater goods / replacements as required in cast iron / matching materials.\nExtensive repairs to the corroded upper roof guardings, external gantries, ladders and elevator leg to make them safe and allow continues access to Silo D.\nRemoval of foliage and graffiti and overpainting those areas in Keim mineral paint in white to match existing.\nRemoval of rotten timber boards to the dock facing terrace and replacements to match.\nRemoval of guano and infilling of openings allowing vermin ingress, with perforated mesh panels. These are temporary works.\nEnsuring the boarded up windows remain sound to exclude vermin and make good/replace as required.\nErection of scaffold for the above works, tied to Silo D as necessary for safety.\n",
